cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PRIS, PSS, or the code in this repository, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "PRIS: Plausibility Rules for Inorganic Structures"
abstract: >-
  Eight one-line laws over quantities computable from a structure file and a radius
  table, discovered by autonomous agents through proposal, test and active refutation.
  They encode five complementary physicochemical mechanisms and are scored on two axes
  at once: satisfaction on experimental crystals and detection of chemically damaged
  ones. PSS, a PRIS-derived synthesis score, extends them to synthesizability screening.
type: software
license: MIT
